        "answer": {
          "short": "$(-1,1)$ and $(3,5)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2-x-1&=x+2\\\\x^2-2x-3&=0\\\\(x-3)(x+1)&=0\\\\x&=3\\text{ or }-1\\end{align*}$$\nWhen $x=3$, $y=3+2=5$. When $x=-1$, $y=-1+2=1$.\nThe points of intersection are $(-1,1)$ and $(3,5)$.",
